# Data Agent MCP Server environment example — public placeholders only.
# Security-remediation implementation is under validation; release gates remain open.
# Loaded from $DATA_AGENT_ENV_FILE, else ./.env, without overriding process env.
# Prefer managed environment injection for secrets and the SDK default chain.
# Secret-bearing .env/YAML/JSON default to process-owned regular files, POSIX
# 0600/0400 in trusted directories; public placeholder-only examples may be 0644.
# Transitional exception: export DOTENV_UNSAFE_FILES_ALLOW=1 in the PROCESS
# environment/launch command, not this .env. Allows root/service-owned,
# non-executable regular files (e.g. 0644), never group/other-writable files.
# Trusted-parent ownership/no-group-other-write checks, final symlink/FIFO rejection
# and Windows rejection without verified ACLs remain. Warns without secret values.
# No automatic chmod/chown/migration; 0644 is not recommended for long-term secrets.
# Obtain admin authorization for real changes. See README.md.

# Optional explicit credentials for the credentials-go default chain.
# Leave these commented/absent for an instance/workload-role or other SDK provider.
# The base principal needs sts:AssumeRole on mapped roles; roles must trust it.
#ALIBABA_CLOUD_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<access-key-id>
#ALIBABA_CLOUD_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET=<access-key-secret>
# Required with AK/SK for temporary credentials:
#ALIBABA_CLOUD_SECURITY_TOKEN=<sts-security-token>
# Static STS env values do not self-renew. Retain a refreshable SDK provider for
# long-running deployments. CLI profiles are not automatically imported.

# Legacy API Key: local stdio single-process only; real-cloud validation pending.
# A nonempty key requires identity.enabled=false and agent_gateway.enabled=false.
# Empty keys/endpoint-only settings do not block SDK AK/STS multi-tenant startup.
#DATA_AGENT_API_KEY=<api-key>
#DATA_AGENT_API_KEY_ENDPOINT=
#DATA_AGENT_API_KEY_STREAM_ENDPOINT=

# Optional overrides (highest priority, above config.yaml).
#DATA_AGENT_REGION=cn-hangzhou
#DATA_AGENT_DMS_UNIT=
#DATA_AGENT_DMS_ENTERPRISE_ENDPOINT=
#DATA_AGENT_ENDPOINT=
#DATA_AGENT_WORKSPACE_ID=
#DATA_AGENT_CUSTOM_AGENT_ID=
#DATA_AGENT_SESSIONS_DIR=
#DATA_AGENT_CONFIG=./config.yaml

# Transport: stdio (default, local only), streamable-http, or sse.
# Set MCP_TRANSPORT explicitly for remote HTTP/SSE; both require identity below.
#MCP_TRANSPORT=stdio
# MCP_PORT is required for streamable-http/sse and unused for stdio.
# Choose an available port on the deployment host; there is no default.
#MCP_PORT=61026

# ALL remote HTTP/SSE deployments require YAML identity.enabled=true,
# require_identity=true (omitted = true; false rejects) and this nonempty token.
# identity.namespace omitted/empty = "default"; explicit valid values unchanged.
# Independent deployments/trust domains sharing sessions_dir need distinct namespaces.
# The server validates this token with gateway on/off on initialize, tools/list,
# tools/call, notifications and every GET/POST/DELETE. No anonymous/global-AK fallback.
# Only trusted upstreams may hold the platform token; never distribute it to end users.
# Header identity requires an upstream that authenticates callers, overwrites their
# identity headers and ensures namespace-wide ID uniqueness; restrict server access
# to trusted upstreams. The token does not verify self-reported end-user identity.
#IDENTITY_AUTH_TOKEN=<platform-auth-token>
# Legacy aliases: AILY_SHARED_SECRET / IDENTITY_SHARED_SECRET.

# With YAML identity.jwt.enabled=true, a completely absent JWT header permits
# trusted Header user/email under shared mappings. A present empty/invalid/expired
# JWT rejects without downgrade. Valid HS256 + exp + user_id or email takes precedence;
# simultaneous plain user/email headers are ignored. Token validation is always required.
# With jwt.enabled=false, any JWT header (even empty) rejects. No new compatibility flag.
# YAML groups/default: ALL exact nonempty tenant/agent pairs, or ALL both omitted/empty.
# Shared mappings accept Header identity and valid JWTs without tenant_id/agent_id;
# match user_id/email in one trusted domain. Explicit scopes require a complete matching
# signed JWT pair; Header cannot match. No mixed/partial/wildcard mapping scopes.
# Header session_name_claim value missing: fall back to user_id, then email. JWT explicitly
# selected non-default claims must exist; only default user_id may fall back to email.
# principal-v2 keeps namespace/auth_mode/scope/typed subject isolation for protocol,
# tenant cache and history. No automatic Header/JWT history merge or v1 migration.
#IDENTITY_JWT_SECRET=<jwt-signing-key>
# HMAC keys are used as-is, not base64-decoded. Additional keys have EQUIVALENT
# signing authority in ONE trusted domain (rotation or mutually trusted apps).
# Not issuer isolation: unrelated issuers need separate instances/configurations
# and distinct namespaces if sharing a sessions root.
#IDENTITY_JWT_SECRETS=<additional-trusted-key>,<rotation-key>

# agent_gateway has no additional gateway token. P2b remains off by default.
# HTTP limits and identity.max_tenants (128 cached + initializing total) use YAML;
# explicit zero/negative limits reject startup, rather than disabling protection.
# dacli runs only in a trusted upstream/operator context. AILY_TOKEN is the platform
# token; AILY_JWT is an issued client JWT, not the server signing secret.
# --config reads identity.auth_token only; it never issues JWTs or loads server env/.env
# overrides. For shared mappings, use --user with no JWT (unset AILY_JWT or --jwt '').
# dacli remains a Streamable HTTP client, not SSE; see README.md for the 8931 example.
